{#
  The booking's own rail (issue #462): one chip per page of its file,
  through the shared partials/page_picker.html.twig (design.md §7.6).

  It REPLACES the asset's rail (`_nav.html.twig`) on these pages rather
  than sitting under it — the breadcrumb is the way back to the asset.

  The pages come from the controller (`booking_pages`, a list of
  Booking\BookingPage) because only it knows whether « Courrier » exists
  here: a chip that does nothing is worse than one that is not there, the
  rule `_nav.html.twig` already follows, so an unavailable page is absent
  rather than disabled. « Séjour » is never one of them: it has its own page
  one level deeper in the breadcrumb, and a chip would put it on this level.

  Requires `booking_pages`, `booking_page` and `booking_url`.
#}
{% set pages = [] %}
{% for page in booking_pages %}
    {% set pages = pages|merge([{url: page.url(booking_url), label: page.label}]) %}
{% endfor %}
{% include 'partials/page_picker.html.twig' with {
    picker_id: 'rental-booking-picker',
    pages: pages,
    current_path: booking_page.url(booking_url),
    sheet_title: 'Choisir une page',
    aria_label: 'Pages de la réservation',
} only %}
